End to end
==========

These run against a deployed daemon, not against the package. The unit tests stub
obol, systemd and Luna; these do not, which is the point.

    bash tests/e2e/on-the-controller.sh

On the controller itself. Needs a shell there: it reads the store, checks the rule
files on disk, and checks that a plugin reload leaves the daemon's process running.

    python3 tests/e2e/over-http.py <controller>

From anywhere that can reach the two ports; the plain one, 8051, is on the loopback
by default and has to be opened for this. Covers the API, the pass-through, the hot
swap, the queue, the roles and the replication documents, and nothing that needs a
shell. Both sign in as the ini account trixd with password trixd, so they belong on a
test controller.

Both leave the store as they found it. Neither is run by pytest: they need a
daemon and a Luna, and a test that quietly passes when there is no daemon is
worse than no test.
